From db3c5978e1b80a1795a2da80ca9356d85b40f6d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:45:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/19] feat(tekton): cancel reads the run and reports its
 state; restart keeps the run's labels and annotations (C14, K8S-16)

tekton_pipelinerun_lifecycle's cancel patched spec.status=Cancelled
without looking at the run and answered "PipelineRun '<name>'
cancelled". For a finished run Tekton's webhook refuses the patch (H-08
did not reproduce because of that), and for a running run the answer
claimed a state Tekton had not reached yet; on the native session
(job 11) the agent spent a read to find out what had happened.

- cancel reads the run first. A run whose Succeeded condition is True or
  False has finished: the answer says so with its reason ("Failed",
  "Succeeded") and nothing is changed. Otherwise spec.status is patched
  and the answer says a cancellation was requested and what Tekton
  does next (C14).
- restart (PipelineRun and TaskRun) copied only the spec, so labels and
  annotations set on the run itself (for example Tekton Triggers'
  eventlistener labels, or a team annotation) were lost (K8S-16, as
  narrowed by the refuter). They are now copied, except Tekton's own
  tekton.dev/ keys, which Tekton sets again from the Pipeline or Task,
  and kubectl's last-applied annotation.

The shared PipelineRun fixture is a failed run; the existing cancel
test now creates a running run, and a new test checks that a finished
run is left alone. Tool descriptions say what each action does now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
